const llmActionsProps = {"enabled":true,"providers":["claude","chatgpt","perplexity","gemini"],"placement":"header","copyButton":true,"footerLink":true,"markdownBody":"# Stage 10: Keys {#stage-10-keys}\n\nDefine keys for the product name, version, download URL, and selected topics. A `<keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>` uses text from a key definition; an `<xref keyref=\"install\"/>` uses a key to identify a link target. Updating the definition changes each reference that resolves to it.\n\nStore product values in `keydefs-product.ditamap` and include that map with `<mapref>`. Define topic keys with `@keys` on the guide's existing `<topicref>` elements.\n\n**Time:** about 30 minutes. **You need:** stage 09 complete.\n\nRecorded output below is an example. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. [Check your work](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/run-the-gate) to see the result for your own project.\n\n## Step 1: Define the product keys {#step-1-define-the-product-keys}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Create `keydefs-product.ditamap`** in `my-audacity-guide`. In the **Explorer**, right-click `my-audacity-guide`, choose **New File**, and enter `keydefs-product.ditamap`. In the **New XML Document** dialog, click **Key Definition Map**. The template contains two sample key definitions:\n\n   ```xml\n   <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n   <!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n   <map>\n     <title>Key Definitions</title>\n     <keydef keys=\"installing\" href=\"topic.dita\"/>\n     <keydef keys=\"product-name\">\n       <topicmeta>\n         <keywords>\n           <keyword>Product Name</keyword>\n         </keywords>\n       </topicmeta>\n     </keydef>\n   </map>\n   ```\n\n   Replace the title with `Product key definitions`. Delete the sample `installing` key definition, because this map defines text and URL keys only; step 2 keys the topics in the guide map. Keep the `product-name` key definition and replace `Product Name` with `Audacity`, then add the other three key definitions. Save the file, so that the build sees it. If you use another editor, create the file and type the finished listing. The finished map:\n\n   ```xml {title=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"}\n   <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n   <!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n   <map>\n     <title>Product key definitions</title>\n\n     <keydef keys=\"product-name\">\n       <topicmeta>\n         <keywords>\n           <keyword>Audacity</keyword>\n         </keywords>\n       </topicmeta>\n     </keydef>\n     <keydef keys=\"product-version\">\n       <topicmeta>\n         <keywords>\n           <keyword>3.4</keyword>\n         </keywords>\n       </topicmeta>\n     </keydef>\n     <keydef keys=\"download-url\" href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/download/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n       <topicmeta>\n         <linktext>the Audacity download page</linktext>\n       </topicmeta>\n     </keydef>\n     <keydef keys=\"project-extension\">\n       <topicmeta>\n         <keywords>\n           <keyword>.aup3</keyword>\n         </keywords>\n       </topicmeta>\n     </keydef>\n   </map>\n   ```\n2. **Read the elements**\n\n   - `<keydef>` is a `<topicref>` specialized for defining keys. `@keys` is the key name. A `<keydef>` with no `@href` defines text only.\n   - The text comes from `<keywords>` inside `<topicmeta>`: the `<keyword>` is what a `<keyword keyref>` in a topic renders as.\n   - `download-url` has an `@href` with `@scope=\"external\"` and `@format=\"html\"`, exactly as an external `<xref>` in stage 07. Its `<linktext>` is the text an empty `<xref keyref=\"download-url\"/>` shows, because a web page has no DITA title to borrow.\n   - A keydef map is an ordinary map with a `<title>`. It is never published on its own; the guide references it.\n:::\n\n## Step 2: Bring the keys into the guide and key the topics {#step-2-bring-the-keys-into-the-guide-and-key-the-topics}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Edit `audacity-guide.ditamap`** After the `<topicmeta>`, add a `<mapref>` and one more `<keydef>`. Then add `@keys` to three `<topicref>` elements that are already in the guide. Save the map.\n\n   ```diff {title=\"audacity-guide.ditamap\"}\n   --- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n   +++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n   @@ -7,11 +7,14 @@\n        <shortdesc>Record, edit and export audio with Audacity, from your first track to a finished file.</shortdesc>\n      </topicmeta>\n\n   +  <mapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>\n   +  <keydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n   +\n      <topichead navtitle=\"Getting started\">\n        <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\">\n   -      <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n   +      <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\" keys=\"digital-audio\"/>\n        </topicref>\n   -    <topicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n   +    <topicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\" keys=\"install\"/>\n      </topichead>\n\n      <topichead navtitle=\"Recording and editing\">\n   @@ -25,7 +28,7 @@\n      </topichead>\n\n      <topichead navtitle=\"Reference\" id=\"reference\">\n   -    <topicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n   +    <topicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n          <topicmeta>\n            <navtitle>Audio formats</navtitle>\n          </topicmeta>\n   ```\n2. **Read the map**\n\n   - `<mapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>` includes another map. Its key definitions join the guide's key space; a `<keydef>` that is not reachable from the root map defines nothing.\n   - `<keydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>` gives a topic a key without adding it to the table of contents: a keydef is `@processing-role=\"resource-only\"` by default.\n   - `@keys` on a `<topicref>` that is already in the guide, such as `keys=\"install\"`, keys the topic in place. The key space is `start-here`, `digital-audio`, `install`, `formats` and the four product keys.\n:::\n\n## Step 3: Use the keys in the topics {#step-3-use-the-keys-in-the-topics}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Key one topic first** Open `topics/installing-audacity.dita`. In the download step, replace `Audacity` and the address after it with `<keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>`, then add `<keyword keyref=\"product-version\"/>` and the link `<xref keyref=\"download-url\"/>`. Do the same in the result, with the name and the version, and in the title. The listing in item 3 shows the finished lines. Leave the rest of the topic for item 3, and save the file.\n\n   The title and the download step now hold empty elements. Predict what the built page shows there. Then choose **Project** > **Check Project**. The check covers the keys too, and it rebuilds the guide in `out/full/`. Open `out/full/topics/installing-audacity.html` and choose **View** > **Preview in Tab**. The title reads *Installing Audacity*, and the download step reads \"Download Audacity 3.4 from the Audacity download page\", with a link to the download address. The words come from the key definitions, not from the topic.\n2. **Change the definition once** In `keydefs-product.ditamap`, change `Audacity` to `Audacity Pro` and save the file. You have not changed the topic. Predict what its title and download step say after the next build. Then choose **Project** > **Check Project** again, and preview the built install page as before. Every reference changed, including the title, *Installing Audacity Pro*, and the download step, \"Download Audacity Pro 3.4\". The table of contents shows the new title too. The short description still says *Audacity*, because it is typed text, not a key.\n\n   Change the name back to `Audacity`, exactly, and save the file. The rest of the course uses it.\n3. **Key the rest of the topics** Every other literal \"Audacity\" becomes `<keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>`, and three links go through keys. In each topic, use **Edit** > **Replace...** to find `Audacity` and replace it with the keyword. Skip the places that must stay literal, such as the Windows install folder, which is a file path, the web addresses, and the title of the quoted manual in *What is digital audio?*, which is an attribute value.\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n   +++ b/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n   @@ -2,19 +2,19 @@\n    <!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n    <task id=\"installing-audacity\">\n   -  <title>Installing Audacity</title>\n   -  <shortdesc>Download Audacity from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.</shortdesc>\n   +  <title>Installing <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/></title>\n   +  <shortdesc>Download <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.</shortdesc>\n      <taskbody>\n        <prereq>\n          <p>You need about 250 MB of free disk space and an account that can install software.</p>\n        </prereq>\n        <context>\n   -      <p>Audacity is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n   +      <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n          The steps differ by operating system only at the install step.</p>\n        </context>\n        <steps>\n          <step>\n   -        <cmd>Download Audacity from <filepath>https://www.audacityteam.org/download/</filepath>.</cmd>\n   +        <cmd>Download <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> <keyword keyref=\"product-version\"/> from <xref keyref=\"download-url\"/>.</cmd>\n            <info>\n              <p>Select the installer for your operating system.</p>\n            </info>\n   @@ -33,7 +33,7 @@\n              </chrow>\n              <chrow>\n                <choption>macOS</choption>\n   -            <chdesc>Open the downloaded <filepath>.dmg</filepath> file and drag Audacity to your <filepath>Applications</filepath> folder.</chdesc>\n   +            <chdesc>Open the downloaded <filepath>.dmg</filepath> file and drag <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> to your <filepath>Applications</filepath> folder.</chdesc>\n              </chrow>\n              <chrow>\n                <choption>Linux</choption>\n   @@ -42,10 +42,10 @@\n            </choicetable>\n          </step>\n          <step>\n   -        <cmd>Launch Audacity.</cmd>\n   +        <cmd>Launch <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>.</cmd>\n            <substeps>\n              <substep>\n   -            <cmd>If Audacity asks to scan for audio plugins, click <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n   +            <cmd>If <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> asks to scan for audio plugins, click <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n                <info>\n                  <p>This happens once, on first launch.</p>\n                </info>\n   @@ -60,7 +60,7 @@\n          </step>\n        </steps>\n        <result>\n   -      <p>Audacity is installed and ready to use.</p>\n   +      <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> <keyword keyref=\"product-version\"/> is installed and ready to use.</p>\n        </result>\n        <postreq>\n          <p>Connect a microphone, then continue with <xref href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>.</p>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n   +++ b/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n   @@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n      <taskbody>\n        <prereq>\n          <p>Finish editing and save the project.\n   -      A project file (<filepath>.aup3</filepath>) can only be opened by Audacity; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.</p>\n   +      A project file (<filepath>.aup3</filepath>) can only be opened by <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.</p>\n        </prereq>\n        <steps>\n          <step>\n   @@ -17,7 +17,7 @@\n            </stepresult>\n          </step>\n          <step>\n   -        <cmd>Choose a format (see <xref href=\"supported-audio-formats.dita#supported-audio-formats/choosing\"/>).</cmd>\n   +        <cmd>Choose a format (see <xref keyref=\"formats/choosing\"/>).</cmd>\n            <choices>\n              <choice>Choose <uicontrol>WAV</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>FLAC</uicontrol> for an archive copy with no quality loss.</choice>\n              <choice>Choose <uicontrol>MP3</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>OGG</uicontrol> for a small file to share.</choice>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n   +++ b/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n   @@ -2,12 +2,12 @@\n    <!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n\n    <concept id=\"what-is-audacity\">\n   -  <title>What is Audacity?</title>\n   -  <shortdesc>Audacity is a free, open-source audio editor and recorder for Windows, macOS and Linux.</shortdesc>\n   +  <title>What is <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>?</title>\n   +  <shortdesc><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is a free, open-source audio editor and recorder for Windows, macOS and Linux.</shortdesc>\n      <conbody>\n   -    <p>Audacity records live audio, imports and exports the common audio formats, and edits sound with cut, copy, paste and a library of effects.\n   +    <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> records live audio, imports and exports the common audio formats, and edits sound with cut, copy, paste and a library of effects.\n        It is free to download and use, and it runs on Windows, macOS and Linux.</p>\n   -    <p>With Audacity you can:</p>\n   +    <p>With <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> you can:</p>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Record live audio through a microphone or mixer.</li>\n          <li>Import and export audio in many formats, including WAV, MP3, OGG and FLAC.</li>\n   @@ -19,12 +19,13 @@\n          <p>Podcasters record and clean up their episodes.\n          Archivists digitize vinyl records and cassettes.\n          Video makers edit sound effects and voice-overs.\n   -      Whatever the project, Audacity provides the tools at no cost.</p>\n   +      Whatever the project, <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> provides the tools at no cost.</p>\n        </section>\n      </conbody>\n      <related-links>\n   +    <link keyref=\"install\"/>\n        <link href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n   -      <linktext>The Audacity website</linktext>\n   +      <linktext>The <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> website</linktext>\n          <desc>Downloads, the manual and the user forum.</desc>\n        </link>\n      </related-links>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n   +++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n   @@ -3,7 +3,7 @@\n\n    <task id=\"recording-your-first-track\">\n      <title>Recording your first track</title>\n   -  <shortdesc>Make your first recording in Audacity: pick a microphone, record, stop and play it back.</shortdesc>\n   +  <shortdesc>Make your first recording in <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>: pick a microphone, record, stop and play it back.</shortdesc>\n      <taskbody>\n        <context>\n          <p>This task walks you through making your first audio recording.\n   @@ -13,9 +13,9 @@\n        </context>\n        <steps>\n          <step>\n   -        <cmd>Open Audacity.</cmd>\n   +        <cmd>Open <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>.</cmd>\n            <info>\n   -          <p>On first launch Audacity opens an empty project window with a gray waveform area.</p>\n   +          <p>On first launch <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> opens an empty project window with a gray waveform area.</p>\n            </info>\n          </step>\n          <step>\n   @@ -44,7 +44,7 @@\n          <step>\n            <cmd>Click <uicontrol>Record</uicontrol>, or press <uicontrol>R</uicontrol>, to start recording.</cmd>\n            <info>\n   -          <p>A blue waveform appears as Audacity captures audio from your microphone, like <xref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita#what-is-digital-audio/fig-waveform\"/>.</p>\n   +          <p>A blue waveform appears as <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> captures audio from your microphone, like <xref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita#what-is-digital-audio/fig-waveform\"/>.</p>\n              <note type=\"warning\">A flat line instead of a waveform means the microphone is not selected correctly.\n              Click <uicontrol>Stop</uicontrol> and check the recording device.</note>\n            </info>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n   +++ b/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n   @@ -3,10 +3,10 @@\n\n    <reference id=\"supported-audio-formats\">\n      <title>Supported audio formats</title>\n   -  <shortdesc>The audio formats Audacity imports and exports, and when to use each one.</shortdesc>\n   +  <shortdesc>The audio formats <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> imports and exports, and when to use each one.</shortdesc>\n      <refbody>\n        <section>\n   -      <p>Audacity imports and exports audio in several formats.\n   +      <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> imports and exports audio in several formats.\n          <term>Lossless</term> formats keep every sample of the source; <term>lossy</term> formats discard detail to make smaller files.\n          Exported files are named after the project, so <filepath>podcast-episode-1.aup3</filepath> exports as <filepath>podcast-episode-1.mp3</filepath>.</p>\n        </section>\n   @@ -72,7 +72,7 @@\n      </refbody>\n      <related-links>\n        <link href=\"https://manual.audacityteam.org/man/file_formats.html\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n   -      <linktext>File formats in the Audacity Manual</linktext>\n   +      <linktext>File formats in the <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> Manual</linktext>\n        </link>\n      </related-links>\n    </reference>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n   +++ b/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n   @@ -37,7 +37,7 @@\n          <step>\n            <cmd>Save the project with <menucascade><uicontrol>File</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd>\n            <info>\n   -          <p>Audacity saves the project as a single <filepath>.aup3</filepath> file in the folder you choose; the <wintitle>Save Project</wintitle> dialog suggests your Documents folder.</p>\n   +          <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> saves the project as a single <filepath>.aup3</filepath> file in the folder you choose; the <wintitle>Save Project</wintitle> dialog suggests your Documents folder.</p>\n            </info>\n          </step>\n        </steps>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n   +++ b/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n   @@ -25,7 +25,7 @@\n          <step>\n            <cmd>Choose <menucascade><uicontrol>Effect</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Removal and Repair</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Reduction</uicontrol></menucascade>, then click <uicontrol>Get Noise Profile</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n            <stepresult>\n   -          <p>Audacity captures the character of the noise and closes the dialog.</p>\n   +          <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> captures the character of the noise and closes the dialog.</p>\n            </stepresult>\n          </step>\n          <step>\n   ```\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n   +++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n   @@ -65,7 +65,7 @@\n            <strow>\n              <stentry>32-bit float</stentry>\n              <stentry>effectively unlimited</stentry>\n   -          <stentry>editing inside Audacity</stentry>\n   +          <stentry>editing inside <keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/></stentry>\n            </strow>\n          </simpletable>\n        </section>\n   ```\n4. **Preview a keyed topic** Open `topics/what-is-audacity.dita` and choose **View** > **Preview in Tab**. The bar above the preview reads **Map: audacity-guide.ditamap**: the preview resolves keys through the map of the active deliverable, `full`, so every `product-name` reference shows as *Audacity*, underlined to mark it as text that comes from a key.\n5. **Read the four forms of reference**\n\n   - `<keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>`: variable text. The element is empty; the processor fills in the `<keyword>` from the keydef. It works in a `<title>` and a `<shortdesc>` as well as in a `<p>`.\n   - `<xref keyref=\"download-url\"/>`: a link through a key to an external page. The text is the keydef's `<linktext>`.\n   - `<xref keyref=\"formats/choosing\"/>`: a link to an element inside a keyed topic. `key/element-id` replaces `file#topic/element-id`; the topic id is not needed because the key already names the topic.\n   - `<link keyref=\"install\"/>`: a related link through a key, with the text taken from the target's title as before.\n   - Keep the example file name `<filepath>podcast-episode-1.aup3</filepath>` literal. Stage 11 uses `project-extension` for the extension itself.\n:::\n\n## Step 4: List the key space {#step-4-list-the-key-space}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Open the key space** Choose **Project** > **Map** > **Key Space...**. The editor resolves the key space of the root map, `audacity-guide.ditamap`, and lists every key with the columns **Key**, **Resolves to**, **Text**, **Defined in** and **Line**. Type in the box above the table to filter the list, and double-click a key to open the map at the line that defines it.\n\n   From the command line, pass the root map to the `keys` command:\n\n   ```bash\n   dogsbay-xml keys audacity-guide.ditamap\n   ```\n\n   ```\n   start-here  →  topics/what-is-audacity.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n   digital-audio  →  topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n   install  →  topics/installing-audacity.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:17]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n   formats  →  topics/supported-audio-formats.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:31]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n   product-name  →  \"Audacity\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:7]\n   product-version  →  \"3.4\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\n   download-url  →  \"the Audacity download page\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:21]\n   project-extension  →  \".aup3\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n   8 key(s).\n   ```\n\n   A topic key shows the file it resolves to; a text key shows its text; each shows the map and line that defines it. Keys from the `<mapref>` are listed as part of the guide's key space.\n:::\n\n## Step 5: Check your work {#step-5-check-your-work}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Format and check your work**\n\n   Save all your files. Format the maps and the topics: choose **Project** > **Project Tools** > **Format Project** to format every file at once, or choose **XML** > **Format** in each changed file and save it. From the command line, run:\n\n   ```bash\n   dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita *.ditamap\n   ```\n\n   Then check the project. In the editor, choose **Project** > **Check Project** and read the result in the **Project Validation** panel. From the command line, run:\n\n   ```bash\n   dogsbay-xml check .\n   ```\n\n   Example output:\n\n   ```\n   health   clean, with warnings\n     unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n     unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15] — nothing references it\n     unused key: project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26] — nothing references it\n   build    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\n   output   clean (full)\n   Ready: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and every link in the pages of full leads somewhere. 3 unused keys above: worth knowing, and not treated as failures.\n   ```\n\n   The three unused keys are defined for later stages: stage 11 uses `project-extension` in a reused step, and stage 18 uses `start-here` and `digital-audio` in a new topic.\n\n   The check builds the guide into `out/full/`. Open `out/full/topics/what-is-audacity.html`, preview it, and scroll to the foot of the page. *Installing Audacity* is among the related links. You wrote only the key. The build took the link text from the task's title, which itself comes from the `product-name` key.\n:::\n\nTest an undefined key reference. Change both occurrences of `keyref=\"product-version\"` in the install task to `product-verson` and check your work. The check stops at health and names both references. Example output:\n\n```\nhealth   NOT CLEAN\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:17  @keyref=\"product-verson\" — key 'product-verson' not defined\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:63  @keyref=\"product-verson\" — key 'product-verson' not defined\n  (run project-health for the full report)\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15] — nothing references it\n  unused key: product-version  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14] — nothing references it\n  unused key: project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26] — nothing references it\nNot ready: the project itself has faults. The build and the built output were not checked.\n```\n\nThe **Project Validation** panel lists the same problems. From the command line, `dogsbay-xml project-health .` prints the full report:\n\n```\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nUndefined keys (2):\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:17  key 'product-verson' not defined\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:63  key 'product-verson' not defined\nUnused keys (4):\n  start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]\n  digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]\n  product-version  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\n  project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n\nSummary\n  Undefined keys                2\n  Unused keys                   4\n```\n\nThe file validates, since `@keyref` is only a name to the DTD, and DITA-OT would build the page with the version missing. The unused keys are warnings. `product-version` appears in the list now because the misspelled references no longer use it.\n\nUndo the change: retype the `i` in both references, save the file, and check again. Confirm that the check reports `Ready`, with only the three unused keys that you saw before, before you continue.\n\n## What you learned {#what-you-learned}\n\n- `<keydef keys=\"…\">` with `<keywords>`/`<keyword>` defines variable text; with `@href` it defines a link target, and `<linktext>` names an external one.\n- `<mapref>` includes a map, keys and all; `@keys` on a `<topicref>` keys a topic in place; a `<keydef>` is resource-only and stays out of the table of contents.\n- `<keyword keyref>`, `<xref keyref>`, `<link keyref>`, and `key/element-id` for an element inside a keyed topic.\n- **Project** > **Map** > **Key Space...**, or `dogsbay-xml keys <rootmap>`, lists the key space; `project-health` reports undefined keys.\n\n## Next lesson {#next-lesson}\n\n**Checkpoint:** `tutorial/10-keys`. If you use Git, commit your work.\n\nContinue with [Stage 11: reuse](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/part-2-maps/stage-11-reuse).\n\nFor the core course, use the [learning path](/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/learning-path) to skip optional modules.\n\n[Compare this stage with its predecessor](https://github.com/dogsbay/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial/compare/tutorial/09-map-structure...tutorial/10-keys).\n","mdUrl":"https://dogsbay.ai/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/part-2-maps/stage-10-keys.md"} ?? undefined;
