      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Preview a keyed topic</strong> Open <code>topics/what-is-audacity.dita</code> and choose <strong>View</strong> &gt; <strong>Preview in Tab</strong>. The bar above the preview reads <strong>Map: audacity-guide.ditamap</strong>: the preview resolves keys through the map of the active deliverable, <code>full</code>, so every <code>product-name</code> reference shows as <em>Audacity</em>, underlined to mark it as text that comes from a key.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the four forms of reference</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keyword keyref="product-name"/&gt;</code>: variable text. The element is empty; the processor fills in the <code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> from the keydef. It works in a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and a <code>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</code> as well as in a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;xref keyref="download-url"/&gt;</code>: a link through a key to an external page. The text is the keydef's <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;xref keyref="formats/choosing"/&gt;</code>: a link to an element inside a keyed topic. <code>key/element-id</code> replaces <code>file#topic/element-id</code>; the topic id is not needed because the key already names the topic.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;link keyref="install"/&gt;</code>: a related link through a key, with the text taken from the target's title as before.</li>
      <li>Keep the example file name <code>&lt;filepath&gt;podcast-episode-1.aup3&lt;/filepath&gt;</code> literal. Stage 11 uses <code>project-extension</code> for the extension itself.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-list-the-key-space" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: List the key space<a href="#step-4-list-the-key-space" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Open the key space</strong> Choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Map</strong> &gt; <strong>Key Space...</strong>. The editor resolves the key space of the root map, <code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>, and lists every key with the columns <strong>Key</strong>, <strong>Resolves to</strong>, <strong>Text</strong>, <strong>Defined in</strong> and <strong>Line</strong>. Type in the box above the table to filter the list, and double-click a key to open the map at the line that defines it.
      <p>From the command line, pass the root map to the <code>keys</code> command:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml keys audacity-guide.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"start-here  →  topics/what-is-audacity.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\ndigital-audio  →  topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\ninstall  →  topics/installing-audacity.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:17]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita\nformats  →  topics/supported-audio-formats.dita   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:31]  file: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\nproduct-name  →  \"Audacity\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:7]\nproduct-version  →  \"3.4\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\ndownload-url  →  \"the Audacity download page\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:21]\nproject-extension  →  \".aup3\"   [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n8 key(s)."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>A topic key shows the file it resolves to; a text key shows its text; each shows the map and line that defines it. Keys from the <code>&lt;mapref&gt;</code> are listed as part of the guide's key space.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-5-check-your-work" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 5: Check your work<a href="#step-5-check-your-work" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong>
      <p>Save all your files. Format the maps and the topics: choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Project Tools</strong> &gt; <strong>Format Project</strong> to format every file at once, or choose <strong>XML</strong> &gt; <strong>Format</strong> in each changed file and save it. From the command line, run:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita *.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then check the project. In the editor, choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> and read the result in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel. From the command line, run:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean, with warnings\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15] — nothing references it\n  unused key: project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26] — nothing references it\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\noutput   clean (full)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and every link in the pages of full leads somewhere. 3 unused keys above: worth knowing, and not treated as failures."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The three unused keys are defined for later stages: stage 11 uses <code>project-extension</code> in a reused step, and stage 18 uses <code>start-here</code> and <code>digital-audio</code> in a new topic.</p>
      <p>The check builds the guide into <code>out/full/</code>. Open <code>out/full/topics/what-is-audacity.html</code>, preview it, and scroll to the foot of the page. <em>Installing Audacity</em> is among the related links. You wrote only the key. The build took the link text from the task's title, which itself comes from the <code>product-name</code> key.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test an undefined key reference. Change both occurrences of <code>keyref="product-version"</code> in the install task to <code>product-verson</code> and check your work. The check stops at health and names both references. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:17  @keyref=\"product-verson\" — key 'product-verson' not defined\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:63  @keyref=\"product-verson\" — key 'product-verson' not defined\n  (run project-health for the full report)\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15] — nothing references it\n  unused key: product-version  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14] — nothing references it\n  unused key: project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26] — nothing references it\nNot ready: the project itself has faults. The build and the built output were not checked."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel lists the same problems. From the command line, <code>dogsbay-xml project-health .</code> prints the full report:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Root map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nUndefined keys (2):\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:17  key 'product-verson' not defined\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:63  key 'product-verson' not defined\nUnused keys (4):\n  start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]\n  digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]\n  product-version  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\n  project-extension  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n\nSummary\n  Undefined keys                2\n  Unused keys                   4"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The file validates, since <code>@keyref</code> is only a name to the DTD, and DITA-OT would build the page with the version missing. The unused keys are warnings. <code>product-version</code> appears in the list now because the misspelled references no longer use it.</p>
      <p>Undo the change: retype the <code>i</code> in both references, save the file, and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code>, with only the three unused keys that you saw before, before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keydef keys="…"&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> defines variable text; with <code>@href</code> it defines a link target, and <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> names an external one.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;mapref&gt;</code> includes a map, keys and all; <code>@keys</code> on a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> keys a topic in place; a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> is resource-only and stays out of the table of contents.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;keyword keyref&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;xref keyref&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;link keyref&gt;</code>, and <code>key/element-id</code> for an element inside a keyed topic.</li>
      <li><strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Map</strong> &gt; <strong>Key Space...</strong>, or <code>dogsbay-xml keys &lt;rootmap&gt;</code>, lists the key space; <code>project-health</code> reports undefined keys.</li>
      </ul>
